From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: opt-in Qualcomm PON reboot-reason write before the PSCI reset

P4 of the agent-control plan: let a reset land directly in
fastboot (or recovery) instead of booting the installed system
first. Before the PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, kreset writes the
reboot-mode field of the pm8998 PON peripheral's SOFT_RB_SPARE
register (SPMI USID 0, register 0x088f): a read-modify-write
(new = (old & 0x01) | field) where field is 0x04 for bootloader
and 0x02 for recovery - the GEN2-shifted magics the phone's own
device tree declares (pon@800 mode-bootloader=<0x02>,
mode-recovery=<0x01>; Linux drivers/power/reset/qcom-pon.c,
qcom_pon_reboot_mode_write).

The register sits behind the SPMI PMIC arbiter, so the patch
adds a minimal arbiter-v5 client (device/qcom_pon.rs): a
VERSION gate (refuse pre-v5), runtime APID discovery for PPID
0x008 with Linux's duplicate-PPID ee-ownership rule, an
observer-channel read, the RMW on the RW channel, a status
poll (1000 us timeout plus a poll-count backstop), and a
read-back verify. Region bases and the PON base come from the
FDT, never literals. The transaction runs against an abstract
bus; the pure layer is host-tested (14 tests: encodings, APID
selection, RMW math, status classification, env parsing).

Opt-in twice over: Cargo feature qcom-pon-reboot-reason
(default OFF, mirroring qcom-dload-mode-clear), and the
request itself arrives in the kernel environment
(REDOX_PON_REBOOT_REASON=bootloader|recovery, forwarded by a
sibling bootloader patch mirroring 0004). Absent or unknown
values still write REASON_NONE, so the field is deterministic
after every feature-enabled reset whether or not the
bootloader clears it after consuming it. Any failure is a
warning; the reset proceeds unchanged. emergency_reset is
untouched. The emulator has no arbiter model, so the gate
proves non-regression only; the write itself is proven by the
attended first device run.

